From: Cage contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: retain process socket through native exit cleanup

Closing fd_socket starts wineserver's process-death timer while libc exit()
can still be running native finalizers. Let kernel descriptor teardown report
process death after native cleanup. Preserve exit(status), all native cleanup,
and Wine's server-side timer; no exit status or application deadline changes.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1594,6 +1594,5 @@
  */
 void process_exit_wrapper( int status )
 {
-    close( fd_socket );
     exit( status );
 }
